#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:5
msgid "XFRM SA Migrate State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:10
msgid ""
"``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` migrates a single SA, looked up using SPI and "
"mark, without involving policies. Unlike ``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE``, which couples "
"SA and policy migration and allows migrating multiple SAs in one call, this "
"interface identifies the SA unambiguously via SPI and supports changing the "
"reqid, addresses, encapsulation, selector, and offload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:16
msgid ""
"Because IKE daemons can manage policies independently of the kernel, this "
"interface allows precise per-SA migration without requiring policy "
"involvement. Optional netlink attributes follow an omit-to-inherit model: "
"omitting an attribute preserves the value from the old SA. The ``flags`` "
"field controls two exceptions: hardware offload is inherited by default and "
"can be suppressed with ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_CLEAR_OFFLOAD`` or overridden "
"with ``XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV``; the new selector is taken from ``new_sel`` by "
"default and can instead be derived from the new addresses with "
"``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_UPDATE_H2H_SEL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:27
msgid "SA Identification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:29
msgid ""
"The struct is defined in ``include/uapi/linux/xfrm.h``. The SA is looked up "
"using ``xfrm_state_lookup()`` with ``id.spi``, ``id.daddr``, ``id.proto``, "
"``id.family``, and ``old_mark.v & old_mark.m`` as the mark key::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:46
msgid ""
"The ``reserved`` field must be set to zero; the kernel rejects any other "
"value with ``-EINVAL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:50
msgid "Supported Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:52
msgid ""
"The following fields in ``xfrm_user_migrate_state`` are always explicit and "
"are not inherited from the existing SA. Passing zero is not equivalent to "
"\"keep unchanged\" — zero is used as-is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:56
msgid "``new_daddr`` - new destination address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:57
msgid "``new_saddr`` - new source address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:58
msgid "``new_family`` - new address family"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:59
msgid "``new_reqid`` - new reqid (0 = no reqid)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:60
msgid ""
"``new_sel`` - new selector; used when ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_UPDATE_H2H_SEL`` "
"is not set (see `Flags`_ below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:62
msgid ""
"``flags`` - bitmask of ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_*`` flags (see `Flags`_ below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:64
msgid ""
"The following netlink attributes are also accepted. Omitting an attribute "
"inherits the value from the existing SA (omit-to-inherit)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:71
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:240
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:72
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:119
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:241
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:73
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:246
msgid "``XFRMA_MARK``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:74
msgid ""
"Mark on the migrated SA (``struct xfrm_mark``). Absent inherits "
"``old_mark``. To use no mark on the new SA, send ``XFRMA_MARK`` with ``{0, 0}"
"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:77
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:242
msgid "``XFRMA_ENCAP``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:78
msgid ""
"UDP encapsulation template; only ``UDP_ENCAP_ESPINUDP`` is supported. Set "
"``encap_type=0`` to remove encap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:80
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:244
msgid "``XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:81
msgid ""
"Hardware offload configuration (``struct xfrm_user_offload``). Absent copies "
"offload from the existing SA. When ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_CLEAR_OFFLOAD`` is "
"set in ``flags``, the new SA has no offload; this flag is mutually exclusive "
"with ``XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV`` and sending both returns ``-EINVAL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:86
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:248
msgid "``XFRMA_SET_MARK``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:87
msgid ""
"Output mark on the migrated SA; pair with ``XFRMA_SET_MARK_MASK``. Send 0 to "
"clear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:89
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:254
msgid "``XFRMA_NAT_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:90
msgid ""
"NAT keepalive interval in seconds. Requires encap. Send 0 to clear. "
"Automatically cleared when encap is removed; setting a non-zero value "
"without encap returns ``-EINVAL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:93
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:252
msgid "``XFRMA_MTIMER_THRESH``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:94
msgid ""
"Mapping maxage threshold. Only valid on input SAs; setting on an output SA "
"returns ``-EINVAL``. Requires encap. Send 0 to clear. Automatically cleared "
"when encap is removed; setting a non-zero value without encap returns ``-"
"EINVAL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:99
msgid ""
"The following SA properties are immutable and cannot be changed via "
"``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE``: algorithms (``XFRMA_ALG_*``), replay state, "
"direction (``XFRMA_SA_DIR``), and security context (``XFRMA_SEC_CTX``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:104
msgid "Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:106
msgid ""
"The ``flags`` field in ``xfrm_user_migrate_state`` controls optional "
"migration behaviour. Unknown flag bits are rejected with ``-EINVAL``; the "
"extended ACK message identifies the unrecognised bits (e.g. ``\"Unknown "
"flags: 0x4\"``). Userspace can use ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_KNOWN_FLAGS`` "
"(defined in ``<linux/xfrm.h>``) to validate flags before sending; note that "
"this constant reflects the flags known to the header version userspace was "
"compiled against, which may differ from what the running kernel accepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:118
msgid "Flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:120
msgid "``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_CLEAR_OFFLOAD``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:121
msgid ""
"When set, the new SA has no hardware offload even when ``XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV`` "
"is absent. Without this flag, omitting ``XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV`` copies the "
"existing offload to the new SA. Mutually exclusive with "
"``XFRMA_OFFLOAD_DEV``; sending both returns ``-EINVAL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:126
msgid "``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_UPDATE_H2H_SEL``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:127
msgid ""
"When set, the kernel validates that the existing SA selector is a single-"
"host entry matching the SA addresses (``prefixlen_s == prefixlen_d`` equal "
"to 32 for IPv4 or 128 for IPv6, and addresses matching ``id.daddr`` and "
"``props.saddr``). If the check passes, the new selector is derived from "
"``new_daddr`` and ``new_saddr`` with the single-host mask for "
"``new_family``. A mismatch returns ``-EINVAL``. When this flag is not set, "
"``new_sel`` is used as-is for the migrated SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:137
msgid "Migration Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:140
msgid "Outgoing SA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:142
msgid ""
"To prevent cleartext traffic leaks, install a block policy before migrating:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:145
msgid "Install a block policy to drop traffic on the affected selector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:146
msgid "Remove the old policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:147
msgid "Call ``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` for each SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:148
msgid "Reinstall the policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:149
msgid "Remove the block policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:151
msgid ""
"If AES-GCM is in use, the block policy also prevents IV reuse during the "
"migration window. For other AEADs this step is not required for IV safety, "
"but skipping it allows a brief cleartext window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:156
msgid "Incoming SA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:158
msgid ""
"No block policy is needed. ``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` atomically transfers "
"the sequence number and replay window from the old SA to the new SA, so the "
"new SA continues replay protection without a gap. Call "
"``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` for each SA directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:163
msgid ""
"When accepting incoming traffic, be liberal during the migration window: "
"packets sent by the remote peer before it completed its own migration may "
"arrive out of order or slightly late. Dropping them unnecessarily causes "
"packet loss. A generous replay window reduces the impact of reordering "
"during migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:170
msgid "Block Policy and IV Safety"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:172
msgid ""
"AES-GCM IV uniqueness is critical: reusing a (key, IV) pair allows an "
"attacker to recover the authentication subkey and forge authentication tags, "
"breaking both confidentiality and integrity. This concern applies to "
"outgoing SAs only — the remote peer controls IV generation on incoming "
"traffic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:178
msgid ""
"``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` atomically copies the sequence number and replay "
"window from the old SA to the new SA and deletes the old SA. The block "
"policy serves two purposes: it prevents cleartext traffic leaks during the "
"migration window, and for AES-GCM it prevents IV reuse by ensuring no "
"outgoing packets are sent under the same key. The atomic copy of the "
"sequence number and replay window complements this — together they eliminate "
"both risks during migration. The atomic copy also serves incoming SAs, "
"ensuring replay protection continues without a gap across the migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:189
msgid "Feature Detection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:191
msgid ""
"Userspace can probe for kernel support by sending a minimal "
"``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` message with a non-zero non-existent SPI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:194
msgid ""
"``-EINVAL``: kernel predates ``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE``; message type is out "
"of range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:196
msgid ""
"``-ENOPROTOOPT``: message type is known but ``CONFIG_XFRM_MIGRATE`` is not "
"enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:198
msgid "``-ESRCH``: supported (SPI not found)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:201
msgid "Userspace Notification on Success"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:203
msgid ""
"On successful migration the kernel multicasts an ``XFRM_MSG_MIGRATE_STATE`` "
"message to the ``XFRMNLGRP_MIGRATE`` group. The fixed header is ``struct "
"xfrm_user_migrate_state`` copied from the request, followed by the same set "
"of netlink attributes that are accepted as input, with the differences noted "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:210
msgid "Differences from the request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:216
msgid "Field / Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:217
msgid "Difference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:218
msgid "``new_sel``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:219
msgid ""
"Contains the actual selector of the newly installed SA, not the ``new_sel`` "
"from the request. When ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_UPDATE_H2H_SEL`` is set the "
"kernel derives the selector from ``new_daddr`` / ``new_saddr``; the caller's "
"``new_sel`` field is ignored in that case. The notification always carries "
"the real selector of the new SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:225
#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:256
msgid "``XFRMA_SA_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:226
msgid ""
"Present in the notification (set from the direction of the new SA) but **not "
"accepted as input** — direction is immutable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:228
msgid "``flags``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:229
msgid ""
"Echoed back as-is. ``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_CLEAR_OFFLOAD`` and "
"``XFRM_MIGRATE_STATE_UPDATE_H2H_SEL`` describe the request that was made, "
"not a property of the resulting SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:234
msgid "Attributes in the notification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:243
msgid "UDP encapsulation template, if configured on the new SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:245
msgid "Hardware offload configuration, if active on the new SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:247
msgid "Mark on the new SA, if set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:249
msgid "Output mark on the new SA, if set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:250
msgid "``XFRMA_SET_MARK_MASK``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:251
msgid "Output mark mask, present together with ``XFRMA_SET_MARK``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:253
msgid "Mapping maxage threshold, if non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:255
msgid "NAT keepalive interval, if non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:257
msgid "Direction of the new SA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:260
msgid "Error Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:262
msgid ""
"If the target SA tuple (new daddr, SPI, proto, new family) is already "
"occupied, the operation returns ``-EEXIST`` before the migration begins. The "
"old SA remains intact and the operation is safe to retry after resolving the "
"conflict."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:267
msgid ""
"If the target SA is deleted before the migration completes, the operation "
"returns ``-ESRCH``. No new SA is installed. Userspace should verify the "
"current SA state before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../networking/xfrm/xfrm_migrate_state.rst:271
msgid ""
"If the multicast notification (``XFRMNLGRP_MIGRATE``) fails to send, the "
"migration itself has already completed successfully and the new SA is "
"installed. The operation returns success, 0, with an extack warning, but "
"listeners will not receive the migration event."
msgstr ""
